<td id="S5.T1.12.7.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="S5.T1.12.7.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1.33</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T1.12.8" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S5.T1.12.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t" rowspan="4"><span id="S5.T1.12.8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Reranking</span></th>
<th id="S5.T1.12.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">None</th>
<td id="S5.T1.12.8.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T1.12.8.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.808</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.12.8.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">0.765</td>
<td id="S5.T1.12.8.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T1.12.8.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.833</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.12.8.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T1.12.8.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1.67</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T1.12.9" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S5.T1.12.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Frequency</th>
<td id="S5.T1.12.9.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.396<sup id="S5.T1.12.9.2.1" class="ltx_sup"><span id="S5.T1.12.9.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">∗</span></sup></td>
<td id="S5.T1.12.9.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.533<sup id="S5.T1.12.9.3.1" class="ltx_sup"><span id="S5.T1.12.9.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">∗∗</span></sup></td>
<td id="S5.T1.12.9.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.585<sup id="S5.T1.12.9.4.1" class="ltx_sup"><span id="S5.T1.12.9.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">∗∗</span></sup></td>
<td id="S5.T1.12.9.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">4.00</td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T1.12.10" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S5.T1.12.10.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Score</th>
<td id="S5.T1.12.10.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.605</td>
<td id="S5.T1.12.10.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="S5.T1.12.10.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">0.792</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.12.10.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.785<sup id="S5.T1.12.10.4.1" class="ltx_sup"><span id="S5.T1.12.10.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">∗</span></sup></td>
<td id="S5.T1.12.10.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">2.67</td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T1.12.11" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S5.T1.12.11.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb">Combined</th>
<td id="S5.T1.12.11.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="S5.T1.12.11.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">0.798</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.12.11.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="S5.T1.12.11.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.822</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.12.11.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="S5.T1.12.11.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">0.814</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.12.11.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="S5.T1.12.11.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1.67</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Jina v4 with native image embeddings achieves the best retrieval quality (0.890 at <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>=16), outperforming text-only Jina v3 by 6.6 percentage points (<math id="S5.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>=0.016, paired <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>-test). Increasing planner queries from 2 to 6 improves performance substantially (0.562<math id="S5.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math>0.787 at <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>=4, +40% relative), as diverse query formulations capture different aspects of the information need. For reranking, the <span id="S5.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Combined</span> strategy provides the most consistent results across retrieval depths, while <span id="S5.SS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Frequency</span>-only yields substantially lower scores (0.396 vs 0.808 at <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>=4; <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math><math id="S5.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>&lt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;</annotation></semantics></math>0.01), demonstrating that retrieval scores contain important complementary information beyond frequency signals.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.3 </span>Context Enhancement</h3>

<div id="S5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
