<td id="S5.T3.12.8.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="S5.T3.12.8.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1.33</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Grok-4.1-fast achieves the best average rank (1.33) across all retrieval depths, with peak performance of 0.908 at <math id="S5.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>=4. The gap between Grok-4.1-fast and GPT-5-nano is highly significant (<math id="S5.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math><math id="S5.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>&lt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;</annotation></semantics></math>0.001), while differences among top-tier models are not statistically significant (<math id="S5.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math><math id="S5.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>&gt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;</annotation></semantics></math>0.1). Gemini-3-pro uniquely supports native image input. Smaller models (GPT-5-nano, avg rank 7.00) show significant degradation, indicating model capacity is critical.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.5 </span>Ensemble Inference</h3>

