</div>
<div id="alg4.l20" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">20:</span>
                
                
                <span id="alg4.l20.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg4.l20.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg4.l21" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">21:</span>
                
                
                <span id="alg4.l21.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg4.l21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l22" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">22:</span>
                
                
              <span id="alg4.l22.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg4.l22.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">function</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluated the context reduction on the WattBot training set (41 questions) using Jina v4 embeddings with 4 planner queries <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> 16 retrievals per query and top-<math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{\text{final}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mtext>final</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{\text{final}}</annotation></semantics></math>=32. Table <a href="#A1.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ Tree Deduplication. ‣ A.2 Retrieval Pipeline ‣ Appendix A Implementation Details ‣ KohakuRAG: A simple RAG framework with hierarchical document indexing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> reports aggregate statistics. Without deduplication, the 4<math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math>16=64 raw matches are truncated to 32, yielding 148K characters of context with substantial redundancy from nodes retrieved by multiple queries. Node-ID dedup removes these cross-query duplicates, reducing context by 35.0%. Tree dedup further removes hierarchical overlap, achieving a cumulative 51.4% reduction (from 148.1K to 72.0K characters) without discarding any unique information, since the parent node already subsumes all descendant text. Although tree deduplication was not enabled in our competition submissions, it provides a practical mechanism for reducing context length in deployment scenarios where LLM context windows or API costs are constrained.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T6" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 6: </span>Context statistics under different deduplication modes (mean <math id="A1.T6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>±</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm</annotation></semantics></math> std over 41 training questions, 4 queries <math id="A1.T6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> 16 retrievals each). Node-ID dedup removes cross-query duplicates (<math id="A1.T6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>−</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-</annotation></semantics></math>35.0%); tree dedup additionally removes hierarchical overlap (<math id="A1.T6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>−</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-</annotation></semantics></math>51.4% cumulative).</figcaption>
