</div>
<div id="alg5.l24" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">24:</span>
                
                
                <span id="alg5.l24.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg5.l24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a,R,0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a,R,0)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg5.l25" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">25:</span>
                
                
              <span id="alg5.l25.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg5.l25.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">function</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Reference Aggregation Strategies.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We support four strategies for combining reference sets across ensemble runs:</p>
<ul id="A1.I5" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I5.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Independent</span>: Majority vote on references separately from answer</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I5.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">AnswerPriority</span>: Collect refs only from runs matching winning answer</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I5.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I5.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I5.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I5.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Union</span>: Union of refs from runs matching winning answer</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I5.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I5.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I5.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I5.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Intersection</span>: Intersection of refs from runs matching winning answer</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Numeric Answer Normalization.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For numeric answers, we parse values and compare within a tolerance:</p>
<ul id="A1.I6" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I6.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I6.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I6.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Parse scientific notation (e.g., “1.5e6” <math id="A1.I6.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> 1,500,000)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I6.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I6.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I6.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Handle common units (e.g., “1.5 MW” <math id="A1.I6.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> 1,500,000 W)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I6.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I6.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I6.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Group answers within 0.1% relative difference as equivalent</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
</section>
